aisha: Heads-up — found a weird hang in the next-mini starter while doing a long streaming generation. It repros when the API key rotates mid-stream. JS SDK stream just stalls, no reconnect.

kevin: Can you paste a tiny repro? is this the hosted API or dedicated?

aisha: Hosted API. Steps: 1) start demo with a long prompt (>= 1024 tokens), 2) trigger token rotation via the auth shim, 3) stream never finishes. Error in client: "Stream closed unexpectedly, no reconnect".

maria: I think i've seen something similar in the llamaindex sample — streaming + auth refresh edge case. :eyes:

sam: do we have telemetry on stream disconnects around that time?

deploy-bot: New deploy queued: branch=devex/stream-repro id=deploy-2337 link=https://ci.redwood-inference.internal/deploy/2337

aisha: Minimal client snippet that reproduces (from the starter):
```js
const res = await RedwoodSDK.generate({
  model: 'rw-std-1',
  prompt: longPrompt,
  stream: true,
  onDelta: (d) => appendToDom(d.text),
})
```
Auth shim does rotation by swapping Authorization header during stream. After rotation, server returns 401 during a chunk and the JS SDK closes the stream without attempting reconnect. Python SDK retries.

kevin: Thanks. Probable cause: JS stream client treats any non-200 chunk as fatal. Quick question: are you using the browser fetch polyfill or node fetch?

aisha: Browser fetch (edge runtime on Vercel).

kevin: Ok — two quick mitigations: 1) bump SDK to 1.2.3 (we pushed a patch that tolerates transient 401s and attempts a short reconnect window), 2) short-term patch in starter: wrap the onDelta handler to buffer and resume if reconnect happens.

maria: can you share the patch snippet? i'll update the starter templates if it looks safe.

kevin: Patch example (client-side):
```js
// helper that tolerates a transient 401 during streaming
async function safeStreamGenerate(opts){
  try{
    return await RedwoodSDK.generate(opts)
  }catch(err){
    if(err.status === 401 && opts.retryOn401){
      // tiny backoff then retry to allow token rotation to finish
      await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, 300))
      return await RedwoodSDK.generate(opts)
    }
    throw err
  }
}

// usage
safeStreamGenerate({ model: 'rw-std-1', prompt: longPrompt, stream: true, retryOn401: true, onDelta: appendToDom })
```

sam: This is good. We should also add a unit/integration test that simulates mid-stream 401s. I'll add to the devex test harness.

aisha: After bumping to 1.2.3 and applying the safeStreamGenerate wrapper the repro disappeared in my manual runs. :tada:

kevin: I'll open a PR against the starter repo to add this helper + a note in the README about auth rotation. Also adding a small e2e that flips the token mid-stream.

maria: Please add a small blurb in the starter's onboarding doc about using ephemeral keys and token rotation caveats. New users keep hitting this.

deploy-bot: Deploy successful: env=staging id=deploy-2337 status=success link=https://staging.redwood-inference.internal/2337

kevin: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-mini-starter/pull/412 — contains SDK bump + safeStream helper + e2e.

aisha: Verified on staging — streaming resumes after a short hiccup now. Thanks y'all.

maria: I'll cherry-pick to the langchain/llamaindex samplekits too.

sam: I'll add the e2e to the eval harness so we don't regress.

aisha: closing this thread, but leaving the PR link in case anyone wants to review the test. :+1:
